  <main_text>
    <l n="1">pœnî dignus est, qui aliorum in-</l>
    <l n="2">jurias, cum prohibere posset, non</l>
    <l n="3">prohibet, quam qui facit. Et se-</l>
    <l n="4">cundum Agapetum in libello ad-</l>
    <l n="5">monitorio ad Justinianum Impera-</l>
    <l n="6">torem paria censentur peccare, &amp;</l>
    <l n="7">peccantes non cohibere.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Nam qui potest obviare, &amp; per-</l>
    <l n="9">turbare perversos, &amp; non facit, ni-</l>
    <l n="10">hil aliud est, quam favere eorum</l>
    <l n="11">impietati. Nec enim caret scrupulo</l>
    <l n="12">societatis occultæ, qui manifesto fa-</l>
    <l n="13">cinori definit obviare.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Ut Cato senior incitans</l>
    <l n="15">magistratus in eos, qui delin-</l>
    <l n="16">querent, puniendos, dictitaret,</l>
    <l n="17">eos, qui possent, nec propulsa-</l>
    <l n="18">rent injurias, lapidibus esse</l>
    <l n="19">obruendos.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">A quo non alieni Imperato-</l>
    <l n="21">res Leo &amp; Anthemius, qui eâ-</l>
    <l n="22">dem pœna officiales, puniri</l>
    <l n="23">volunt, qui illicitas actiones</l>
    <l n="24">non prohibent, &amp; sic in omit-</l>
    <l n="25">tendo delinquunt, quâ illi, qui</l>
    <l n="26">eas facere ausi fuerint. Con-</l>
  </main_text>
